[138.509592, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[KPerfect! Let me verify the files are all in place:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;208m\u25b6 \u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;35m\u25cf \u001b[39m\u001b[2mRan bash(-rw-rw-r-- 1 ccamacho ccamacho 2.0K Nov 13 18:4...) 0.0s\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KExcellent! All three files are created and the tests pass completely. Here's a summary:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u2713 Task Complete\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mCreated three files:\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K1. \u001b[1mconverter.py\u001b[22m (69 lines) \u2014 Original implementation with duplicated validation logic\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 Each of the three conversion functions (celsius_to_fahrenheit, celsius_to_kelvin,\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kcelsius_to_rankine) contains its own inline validation:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K    \u25aa Type check: ensures input is a number\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K    \u25aa Range check: ensures input \u2265 -273.15\u00b0C (absolute zero)\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K2. \u001b[1mconverter_refactored.py\u001b[22m (67 lines) \u2014 Refactored version with extracted validation\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 Single _validate() helper function encapsulates all shared validation logic\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 All three conversion functions now call _validate() at the start\r\r\n\u001b[5G\u001b[KCleaner, more maintainable code with zero duplication\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K3. **`verify.py`** (118 lines) \u2014 Comprehensive test script\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500